In order to prevent accidents at the edges and openings, which are the main causes of fatal accidents in the construction industry, in this study, the types of accidents at the openings are based on the occupational accident cases of the Korea Industrial Safety and Health Corporation. We conducted disaster statistics analysis and Bow-Tie risk assessment analysis to identify the causes, and confirmed additional measures to prevent the occurrence of accidents. As a result of analyzing the accident caused by the opening, in order to prevent this due to the opening cover not being installed, the opening cover being insufficiently strong, and the opening protection facility being left unattended after random dismantling, the opening cover is covered from the construction stage. We try to provide an alternative by integrating the construction.&#xD;
